==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Psetta maxima Luc Viatour.jpg|thumb|{{taxlink|Scophthalmus maximus|species|noshow=1|ver=161026}}]]

===Etymology===
From Old (and modern) {{etyl|fr|en}} ''{{l|fr|turbot}}'', from {{etyl|gmq-osw|en}} ''[[tornbut]]'', from ''[[törn]]'' (“thorn”) + ''[[but]]'' (“butt, flatfish”).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈtɜːbət/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/ˈtɝbət/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|turbot|turbots}}

# A species of [[flatfish]] native to Europe ({{taxlink|Scophthalmus maximus|species|noshow=1|ver=161026}}, earlier {{taxlink|Psetta maxima|species|noshow=1|ver=161026}}).
# Any of various other [[flatfish]]es of family {{l|mul|Scophthalmidae}} that are found in marine or brackish waters.
#* {{quote-book|year=1931|author=[[w:John Palmer (author)|Francis Beeding]]
|title=Death Walks in Eastrepps
|chapter=1/1|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL6342782W
|passage=Eldridge closed the despatch-case with a snap and, rising briskly, walked down the corridor to his solitary table in the dining-car. Mulligatawny soup, poached '''turbot''', roast leg of lamb—the usual railway dinner.}}
# [[triggerfish|Triggerfish]], {{taxlink|Canthidermis sufflamen|species|noshow=1|ver=161026}}.

